      "body": "## Summary\n\n- give the OpenAI LM-eval correctness server 600 seconds to become healthy on every platform\n- keep TPU behavior unchanged while extending the NVIDIA fallback from 480 to 600 seconds\n\n## Why\n\nThe exact H200 LM-eval test has repeatedly exhausted the fixed 480-second server-start budget while normal initialization was still progressing:\n\n- daily main [#88612](https://buildkite.com/vllm/ci/builds/88612): `test_lm_eval_accuracy_v1_engine` failed after 518.71 seconds; its exact retry passed\n- daily main [#88685](https://buildkite.com/vllm/ci/builds/88685): the same test failed after 521.52 seconds; CUDA-graph capture completed about 15 seconds after timeout cleanup began\n- main [#98836](https://buildkite.com/vllm/ci/builds/98836): H200 OpenAI API Correctness timed out at the same 480-second boundary after a 356-second graph capture\n- main [#98857](https://buildkite.com/vllm/ci/builds/98857): H200 OpenAI API Correctness and Rust Frontend Core Correctness ran concurrently on two `h200-ci-5` MIG slices, spent 203 and 219 seconds in their first graph captures, and both reached the same 480-second boundary\n\nBoth exact lanes passed on intervening main [#98843](https://buildkite.com/vllm/ci/builds/98843), which rules out a deterministic source regression and points to variable host contention/cold-start time. This change adds two minutes of headroom for those slow but healthy starts. Fast starts do not wait longer, and no serving or model-output behavior changes.\n\n## Duplicate work\n\nI searched open vLLM PRs and issues for `test_lmeval`, `max_wait_seconds`, `OpenAI API Correctness timeout`, and `server failed to start`; I found no other open fix for this test's startup budget.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `uvx --python 3.12 pre-commit run --files tests/entrypoints/openai/correctness/test_lmeval.py` (all applicable hooks passed)\n- `git diff --check`\n\nExact H200 `OpenAI API Correctness` and `Rust Frontend Core Correctness` validation is still required. This draft must receive human review of every changed line before promotion.\n\n## AI assistance\n\nOpenAI Codex assisted with CI diagnosis, the code change, validation, and PR preparation under the submitter's direction.\n",
      "changedFiles": 1,
